From: Marionette AirDrop driver research
Subject: [EXPERIMENTAL] cfg80211: opt-in AWDL data-frame submission

cfg80211_mlme_mgmt_tx() rejects every frame that is not a management frame:

	if (!ieee80211_is_mgmt(mgmt->frame_control))
		return -EINVAL;

That line is the last thing standing between an AWDL data frame (three
address 802.11 data carrying LLC/SNAP 00:17:f2/08/00) and the only
transmit path the firmware accepts.  The exception path that candidates
0034-0042 explored is refused by the firmware itself with an unchanging
SFR assert (cmnos_thread_patch.c:1170 ... line#2834), and the STA-vdev
carrier additionally trips a host assertion in dp_tx_hw_enqueue_be()
because tx_exc_metadata->tx_encap_type must be CDP_INVALID_TX_ENCAP_TYPE
or the vdev's own type.

wlan_hdd_mgmt_tx() does not validate the frame type: it only special-cases
authentication frames and otherwise forwards the caller's bytes to
wlan_cfg80211_mgmt_tx() -> WMI MGMT_TX, the native command every P2P
action frame already uses.  So relaxing this one check lets the firmware
transmit arbitrary AWDL bytes without touching the exception path.

Default off, and even when compiled in it needs the root-only
marionette_awdl_mgmt_tx=1 runtime parameter.  The gate is narrow: station
interface, data frame, and the exact Apple AWDL LLC/SNAP prefix.

Depends on 0002 (CONFIG_CFG80211_MARIONETTE_AWDL and the action-frame gate).

Verified on fuxi with driver patch 0044: an AWDL data frame sent during a
remain-on-channel to 2412 was ACKed by an AP that exists only on that
channel, which proves over-the-air delivery rather than host acceptance.

--- a/net/wireless/mlme.c
+++ b/net/wireless/mlme.c
@@ -644,6 +644,48 @@
                 "Experimental AWDL vendor action TX; default off");
 #endif
 
+/* Marionette (0043): AWDL data frames through the management path.
+ *
+ * cfg80211_mlme_mgmt_tx() refuses anything that is not a management frame:
+ *
+ *     if (!ieee80211_is_mgmt(mgmt->frame_control))
+ *             return -EINVAL;
+ *
+ * That single line is what keeps an AWDL *data* frame (three-address 802.11
+ * data carrying LLC/SNAP 00:17:f2/08/00) out of the only transmit path the
+ * firmware accepts.  The exception path that this project spent candidates
+ * 0034-0042 on is refused by the firmware itself with an unchanging SFR
+ * assert, and the STA-vdev carrier additionally trips a host assertion in
+ * dp_tx_hw_enqueue_be() because tx_encap_type must be
+ * CDP_INVALID_TX_ENCAP_TYPE or the type of the vdev carrying it.
+ *
+ * wlan_hdd_mgmt_tx() does NOT validate the frame type: it only special-cases
+ * authentication frames and otherwise hands the caller's bytes to
+ * wlan_cfg80211_mgmt_tx() -> WMI MGMT_TX.  So if cfg80211 lets the frame
+ * through, the firmware receives a native, supported "transmit these bytes"
+ * command instead of a TQM-bypass exception frame.
+ *
+ * The gate is deliberately narrow: station interface, root-only runtime
+ * parameter, data frame, and the exact Apple AWDL LLC/SNAP prefix.
+ */
+static bool cfg80211_marionette_awdl_data(struct wireless_dev *wdev,
+					  struct cfg80211_mgmt_tx_params *params)
+{
+#ifdef CONFIG_CFG80211_MARIONETTE_AWDL
+	static const u8 awdl_snap[8] = { 0xaa, 0xaa, 0x03, 0x00,
+					 0x17, 0xf2, 0x08, 0x00 };
+	const struct ieee80211_mgmt *mgmt = (const void *)params->buf;
+
+	return READ_ONCE(marionette_awdl_mgmt_tx) &&
+		wdev->iftype == NL80211_IFTYPE_STATION &&
+		params->len >= 24 + 16 &&
+		ieee80211_is_data(mgmt->frame_control) &&
+		!memcmp(params->buf + 24, awdl_snap, sizeof(awdl_snap));
+#else
+	return false;
+#endif
+}
+
 static bool cfg80211_marionette_awdl_action(struct wireless_dev *wdev,
 					 struct cfg80211_mgmt_tx_params *params)
 {
@@ -682,7 +724,8 @@
 
 	mgmt = (const struct ieee80211_mgmt *)params->buf;
 
-	if (!ieee80211_is_mgmt(mgmt->frame_control))
+	if (!ieee80211_is_mgmt(mgmt->frame_control) &&
+	    !cfg80211_marionette_awdl_data(wdev, params))
 		return -EINVAL;
 
 	stype = le16_to_cpu(mgmt->frame_control) & IEEE80211_FCTL_STYPE;
